---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import TestimonialsContact from '../components/testimonials-contact.astro';
import ServiceDetailLeft from '../components/service_detail_left.astro';
import ProjectCarousel from '../components/project-carousel.astro';
import Quote from '../components/quote-request.astro';

// SEO Meta Data - Laminate 专页（Sydney）
const title = "Laminate Floor Dent Repair Sydney | Chip & Impact Damage Fix";
const description =
  "Professional laminate floor dent repair in Sydney. We repair chips, dents, gouges and surface damage on laminate flooring without board replacement. On-site, cost-effective laminate floor restoration.";
const keyword =
  "laminate floor dent repair Sydney, laminate floor repair Sydney, laminate chip repair, laminate floor damage repair, laminate flooring restoration Sydney, invisible laminate floor repair";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} {keyword}>
  <Header />

  <section class="page-header">
    <div
      class="page-header__bg"
      style="background-image: url(/assets/images/backgrounds/page-header-bg-service-laminate-floor.jpg);"
    ></div>
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Laminate Floor Dent Repair Sydney</h1>
      <p style="color: white; font-size: 1.2rem;">
        Cost-Effective Repairs for Chips, Dents & Surface Damage
      </p>

      <div class="wallox-breadcrumb">
        <ul class="wallox-breadcrumb__list list-unstyled">
          <li><a href="/"><i class="icon-home"></i> Home</a></li>
          <li><span>Services</span></li>
          <li><span>Laminate Floor Repair Sydney</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="service-details">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row gutter-y-30">
        <ServiceDetailLeft activeHref="/laminate-floor-dent-repair-sydney/" />

        <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-8">
          <div class="service-details__content">
            <div
              class="service-details__thumbnail wow fadeInUp"
              data-wow-duration="1500ms"
              data-wow-delay="300ms"
            >
              <img
                src="/assets/images/service/service-detail-floor-repair.jpg"
                alt="Laminate Floor Dent Repair Sydney"
              />
            </div>

            <h2 class="service-details__title wow fadeInUp">
              Expert Laminate Floor Dent & Chip Repair in Sydney
            </h2>
            <p class="service-details__text wow fadeInUp">
              Laminate flooring is durable and affordable, but once it is chipped or dented,
              the damage can be highly visible and difficult to ignore.
              At <strong>Refinish</strong>, we provide
              <strong>specialised laminate floor repair services in Sydney</strong>,
              restoring damaged areas without replacing entire boards or sections.
            </p>

            <p class="service-details__text wow fadeInUp">
              Our repair techniques are designed specifically for
              <strong>laminate flooring surfaces</strong>,
              recreating colour, pattern, and texture so the repaired area blends naturally
              with the surrounding floor.
              This makes our service ideal for homeowners, landlords, and rental properties.
            </p>

            <p class="service-details__text wow fadeInUp">
              One of the most common situations we encounter is damage discovered during a tenancy changeover — a chip near the kitchen, a dent in the hallway from a moved fridge, or a gouge left by a furniture leg. In most cases, these can be repaired on the same day without touching the surrounding boards. We carry a full range of fill compounds and tinting pigments on the van, so colour matching is done on-site rather than guessed in a workshop.
            </p>

            <h2 class="service-details__title wow fadeInUp">
              Laminate Floor Damage We Repair
            </h2>
            <ul class="wow fadeInUp">
              <li><strong>Dents & Impact Damage:</strong> Caused by dropped objects or heavy furniture.</li>
              <li><strong>Surface Chips:</strong> Along edges, joins, and high-traffic areas.</li>
              <li><strong>Gouges & Cracks:</strong> From sharp impacts or improper installation.</li>
              <li><strong>Lifted or Broken Corners:</strong> Localised board edge damage.</li>
              <li><strong>Visible Wear Spots:</strong> Loss of decorative layer in walkways.</li>
              <li><strong>Scratch Clusters:</strong> Pet claws, chair legs, or gritty foot traffic across high-use zones.</li>
              <li><strong>Water Stain Edges:</strong> Surface discolouration around swollen join areas where moisture has wicked in.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="service-details__title wow fadeInUp">
              Our Laminate Floor Repair Process
            </h2>
            <ol class="service-details__text">
              <li>
                <strong>Damage Assessment:</strong>
                We inspect the laminate layer and determine the most suitable repair method.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Surface Preparation:</strong>
                The damaged area is cleaned and stabilised for optimal adhesion.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Precision Filling:</strong>
                Hard-setting repair compounds are applied and levelled flush with the floor.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Colour & Pattern Matching:</strong>
                We recreate the laminate's printed design for a seamless appearance.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Protective Sealing:</strong>
                A durable top layer is applied to protect against future wear.
              </li>
            </ol>

            <h2 class="service-details__title wow fadeInUp">
              Why Repair Laminate Floors Instead of Replacing Boards?
            </h2>
            <div class="service-details__feature">
              <div class="row wow fadeInUp" data-wow-duration="1500ms" data-wow-delay="300ms">
                <div class="col-lg-6"><div class="service-details__left">
                  <ul class="service-details__list list-unstyled">
                    <li class="service-details__list__item">
                      <div class="service-details__list__icon"><i class="icon-check"></i></div>
                      <span class="service-details__list__text">
                        Significantly Cheaper Than Board Replacement
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="service-details__list__item">
                      <div class="service-details__list__icon"><i class="icon-check"></i></div>
                      <span class="service-details__list__text">
                        No Matching Spare Boards Required
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="service-details__list__item">
                      <div class="service-details__list__icon"><i class="icon-check"></i></div>
                      <span class="service-details__list__text">
                        Minimal Disruption – Repairs Done On-Site
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="service-details__list__item">
                      <div class="service-details__list__icon"><i class="icon-check"></i></div>
                      <span class="service-details__list__text">
                        Ideal for Rental Bond & Pre-Sale Repairs
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="service-details__list__item">
                      <div class="service-details__list__icon"><i class="icon-check"></i></div>
                      <span class="service-details__list__text">
                        No Need to Move All Furniture or Vacate the Property
                      </span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="service-details__list__item">
                      <div class="service-details__list__icon"><i class="icon-check"></i></div>
                      <span class="service-details__list__text">
                        Avoids the Risk of Damaging Adjacent Boards During Removal
                      </span>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div></div>
                <div class="col-lg-6">
                  <div class="service-details__thumb">
                    <img
                      src="/assets/images/service/service-1-9.png"
                      alt="Laminate Floor Repair Sydney"
                    />
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="service-details__title wow fadeInUp">
              Laminate Floor Repair Sydney – FAQs
            </h2>
            <div
              class="faq-page__accordion wallox-accrodion wow fadeInUp"
              data-wow-duration="1500ms"
              data-wow-delay="700ms"
              data-grp-name="wallox-accrodion"
            >
              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    Can laminate floor dents be repaired?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      Yes. Most dents and chips in laminate flooring can be repaired
                      without replacing boards, as long as the damage is localised.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion active">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    Will the repair be visible after it's finished?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      Our colour and pattern matching process ensures the repaired area
                      blends naturally with your existing laminate floor.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    My laminate floor was installed 5 years ago — can you still find a matching replacement board?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      In most cases, no. Laminate flooring ranges are discontinued within a few years, and even if the same product name is still sold, different production batches have slight colour and texture variations that make new boards look mismatched next to aged ones. Unless you kept leftover boards from the original installation, finding a true match is very difficult. This is exactly why on-site repair — blending the existing surface — produces a far better result than trying to source and slot in a replacement board.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    How long does a laminate floor repair take?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      Most single-area repairs — a chip, a dent, or a small gouge — take between 45 minutes and 2 hours. The floor is walkable again the same day once the sealant has cured. For multiple damage points across a large area, we can usually complete everything in one visit.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    Can you repair laminate that has lifted or is swollen from water?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      It depends on the extent of the moisture damage. Minor edge swelling or surface discolouration from a small water incident can often be treated and blended. However, if the core board has fully buckled or the subfloor underneath is saturated, those sections will need to be replaced rather than repaired. We assess this on-site and give you an honest recommendation — we won't attempt a repair that won't hold.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    I'm a tenant moving out — will a repaired chip pass the final inspection?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      Yes, in the vast majority of cases. Property managers check for visible damage, not microscopic imperfections. A professional repair blends the colour and texture well enough that it is not flagged during a standard outgoing inspection. We regularly work with tenants in the 24–48 hours before a vacate, and our repairs consistently pass. That said, we always recommend sending us a photo first so we can assess the damage and give you a realistic expectation before you book.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    Do you repair all laminate brands and thicknesses?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      Yes. We work across standard AC3 and AC4 laminate, high-gloss surfaces, embossed wood-look finishes, and thicker 12mm boards. The repair approach and materials are adjusted based on the surface texture and sheen level of your specific floor. If you have an unusual finish — such as a hand-scraped or deeply embossed board — send us a photo first and we can confirm the best approach.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="accrodion">
                <div class="accrodion-title">
                  <h4 class="accrodion-title__text">
                    <span class="accrodion-title__icon"></span>
                    How do I get a quote for laminate floor repair in Sydney?
                  </h4>
                </div>
                <div class="accrodion-content">
                  <div class="inner">
                    <p class="inner__text">
                      The easiest way is to text a few photos of the damage to <strong>0452 288 855</strong>. Include a shot showing the full board for context and a close-up of the damaged area. We can usually give you a price estimate within a few hours without needing to visit first.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-one" style="padding: 60px 0; background: #222; color: #fff; text-align: center;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Need a Laminate Floor Repair Quote in Sydney?</h2>
      <p>
        Text a photo of your laminate floor damage to
        <strong>0452 288 855</strong> for a fast, free estimate.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="thm-btn" style="margin-top: 20px;">
        Get My Free Quote
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ProjectCarousel category="Floor" />
  <TestimonialsContact />
  <Quote />
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>